{"title":"Cool Anatomical Sculptures of Lego People","link":"https://kottke.org/25/07/cool-anatomical-sculptures-of-lego-people-1","date":1752096746000,"content":"\n        <p>Artist <a href=\"http://www.moistproduction.com\">Jason Freeny</a> is making these neat anatomical sculptures of Lego people.</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/lego-anatomy.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/lego-anatomy.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/lego-anatomy.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" alt=\"Lego Anatomy\" /></p>\n\n<p>You can see more of his work in progress <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/GummiFetus\">on his Facebook page</a>. Reminds me of <a href=\"http://www.etsy.com/shop/mpaulus\">Michael Paulus’ work</a>. (via <a href=\"http://www.thisiscolossal.com/2012/06/jason-freenys-giant-dissected-lego-men/\">colossal</a>)</p>\n\n         <p><em>[This is a vintage post originally from Jun 2012.]</em></p>\n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Jason%20Freeny\">Jason Freeny</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Lego\">Lego</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/timeless%20posts\">timeless posts</a></p>\n\n        \n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"f79fcc52bff91fb3a59efe5f1a49d741433fa4fe8159d6699884e0ae793b2d3b","category":"Sites"}